@startuml bring-up-team
title Companion to M-DP1: operator-signed standing team bring-up (specified-but-unpublished)
actor "Operator" as O
participant "Dispatcher core\nservice UID swarma-dispatcher" as D
database "Dispatcher-owned input, agent/1,\neffects and journal" as J
participant "swarma-user-manager\nroot; account ledger" as H
participant "Credential broker\nunprivileged; bindings and grants" as B
O -> D : operator-signed standing team description\nswarma-dispatcher team/1 (unpublished)
D -> D : authenticate operator; verify signed description; check authority, quotas and leaf constructibility
alt not operator or absent / invalid operator signature
  break no team effect
    D --> O : refuse; agent.spawn is insufficient
  end
else operator-signed description admitted
  D -> J : lock; retain signed input and per-role allocation/effect records
end
loop each described standing role: label, profile, harness, accounts, capabilities
  D -> J : reconcile existing allocation and journaled effects (§§4.6, 7.1)
  alt observation unknown or contradictory
    D -> J : retain pending; retry observation; no duplicate effect or allocation
  else existing standing allocation
    D -> D : reconcile authorised effects with fresh authority checks
    D -> J : retain allocation; no automatic retirement / re-creation or relaunch
  else initial allocation creation admitted
    D -> J : provisioning; standing designation; no expires_at or lifetime quota
    D -> J : journal distinct per-allocation create effect intent (§4.5)
    D -> B : revocation.check exact chains, context prepare
    B --> D : not_revoked / revoked / unavailable + sequence
    alt revoked / unavailable
      break no new effect
        D -> J : retain pending; refuse before create
      end
    end
    D -> H : user.create with recorded create effect ID
    alt create confirmed present
      H --> D : uid, generation
      opt helper v1
        D -> H : fw.apply with its own journaled effect ID
      end
      D -> D : construct narrowed leaf; keep caller dependency (§3.4)
      D -> J : journal distinct bind effect intent
      D -> B : bind with recorded bind effect ID
      alt bind confirmed
        B --> D : binding_id
        D -> J : allocation idle; one standing allocation for this role
      else bind refused / observation unknown or contradictory
        D -> J : provisioning pending; effect.observe with original request_id / operation / canonical argument digest; no automatic retirement
      end
    else create refused / observation unknown or contradictory
      D -> J : provisioning pending; effect.observe with original request_id / operation / canonical argument digest; no duplicate creation
    end
  end
end
D --> O : current per-role allocation / reconciliation result (format unpublished)
note over O,J
  Repeated bring-up and recovery reuse recorded effects: one logical bring-up effect / allocation per role.
  Retirement / re-creation requires the operator's signed record (§5.4).
  Sweep never expires standing allocations; execution start is separate (§5.3).
  Their executions have no max_runtime quota or deadline; sweep never stops them for runtime.
  Explicit stop, operator action, own exit or incident hard stop still ends an execution.
  Direct workers and operator-enrolled orchestrators initially; recursive bootstrap remains gated.
  Requester signs new orchestrator delegation; dispatcher verifies/records, never signs it.
  Signature grammar, remaining fields, role matching and change handling,
  standing designation encoding and signed-record format are unspecified (§16).
  This view does not publish request members, refusal codes or result values.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: [[https://github.com/relux-works/swarma-dispatcher/blob/main/spec/dispatcher.md#55-bring-up-team-specified-but-unpublished §5.5 bring up team]]
  §§3.5, 4.3, 4.5–4.6, 5.4, 7, 16
endlegend
@enduml
